IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ntjcxv-dates`
IMPORT `ntjcxv-claims`

-- Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (NT) -- worked cases for the questions of a party to a civil
-- proceeding.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the text before the file was run; none was copied from the encoding's output. All facts are HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Copyright in Northern Territory legislation is owned by the Northern Territory; quoted under the NT
-- copyright policy of 8 October 1996 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md). This is not an official version of the Act.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Short names for the facts used below`

`NTSC` MEANS `the Supreme Court of the Northern Territory`
`other SC` MEANS `the Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory`
`FCWA` MEANS `the Family Court of Western Australia (a State Family Court)`
`FCA` MEANS `the Federal Court of Australia`
`FamCA` MEANS `the Family Court of Australia`
`elsewhere` MEANS `another court or tribunal`

`MORE APPROPRIATE` MEANS `the court finds it more appropriate that the other court decide it`
`INTERESTS OF JUSTICE` MEANS `the court finds it otherwise in the interests of justice that the other court decide it`
`NEITHER` MEANS `the court finds neither`

`para a to e` MEANS `paragraph (a), (b), (c), (d) or (e) of the Commonwealth Act's definition`
`para ab` MEANS `paragraph (ab) of the Commonwealth Act's definition`
`para unnamed` MEANS `another paragraph of the Commonwealth Act's definition, which s 6(2) does not name`
`no SFM` MEANS `no special federal matter`

`ACL listed` MEANS `the Australian Consumer Law as a law of the Commonwealth: Part 3-1 Division 1, 2, 4 or 5, Part 3-3 or Part 3-4`
`TPA Part V` MEANS `Part V, Division 1 or 1A of the Trade Practices Act 1974`
`ACL other` MEANS `another provision of the Australian Consumer Law (for example Part 3-5, liability of manufacturers for goods with safety defects)`
`no consumer law` MEANS `none of these`

`1 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 3 2026
`28 Feb 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 28 2 2026
`15 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 3 2026
`29 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 29 3 2026
`30 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 30 3 2026
`31 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 31 3 2026

-- Answers, named once so that each assertion reads as a line.
`not under Act s 5` MEANS `not under this Act: a criminal proceeding (s 3(1)) or the Corporations Act jurisdiction (s 3A) (the text's no) -- s 5`
`s 5 no` MEANS `no: on the court's view s 5 does not require the transfer (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
`s 5 nothing` MEANS `this Act does not provide for that transfer; the cross-vesting Act of the Commonwealth or of a State may (NOTHING-kind)`
`s 5(1) yes` MEANS `yes: the Supreme Court must transfer it to the Federal Court or the Family Court, as the case may be (s 5(1))`
`s 5(2) yes` MEANS `yes: the Supreme Court must transfer it to that other Supreme Court (s 5(2)); by s 3(2) that includes the Family Court of Western Australia`
`s 5(3) yes` MEANS `yes: that court must transfer it to the Supreme Court of the Northern Territory (s 5(3))`
`s 5(4) yes` MEANS `yes: the Federal Court or the Family Court must transfer it to the Supreme Court of the Northern Territory (s 5(4))`
`s 5(5) yes` MEANS `yes: the Federal Court or the Family Court must transfer it to the other of them (s 5(5))`

`appeal 7(1) no` MEANS `no: an appeal from a single judge of the Federal Court or the Family Court does not lie to the Full Court of the Supreme Court (s 7(1), the text's no)`
`appeal 7(2) no` MEANS `no: an appeal does not lie from the Federal Court or the Family Court to the other of them (s 7(2), the text's no)`
`appeal 7(3) yes` MEANS `yes: with no matter under a Schedule Act, the appeal is instituted in the Full Court of the Supreme Court and only there (s 7(3))`
`appeal 7(3) no` MEANS `no: with no matter under a Schedule Act, the appeal must be instituted only in the Full Court of the Supreme Court (s 7(3), the text's no)`
`appeal 7(4) yes` MEANS `yes: with a matter under a Schedule Act, the appeal goes only to the Full Court of the Federal Court or of the Family Court, as the case requires, or with special leave to the High Court (s 7(4))`
`appeal 7(4) no` MEANS `no: with a matter under a Schedule Act, the appeal must go to the Full Court of the Federal Court or of the Family Court, or with special leave to the High Court (s 7(4), the text's no)`
`appeal 7(5)` MEANS `the appeal may be dealt with as if no matter in it arose under a Schedule Act (s 7(5))`
`appeal nothing` MEANS `this Act does not say where this appeal goes (NOTHING-kind)`

`NTSC judge` MEANS `a decision of a single judge of the Supreme Court of the Northern Territory`
`FCA judge` MEANS `a decision of a single judge of the Federal Court`
`FamCA judge` MEANS `a decision of a single judge of the Family Court of Australia`
`FCWA judge` MEANS `a decision of a judge of a State Family Court (the Family Court of Western Australia)`
`NT Full Court` MEANS `the Full Court of the Supreme Court of the Northern Territory (the Court of Appeal)`
`FCA Full Court` MEANS `the Full Court of the Federal Court`
`FamCA Full Court` MEANS `the Full Court of the Family Court of Australia`
`High Court` MEANS `the High Court, with special leave`

`s 10 yes` MEANS `yes: the court it is in may transfer it to that lower Northern Territory court, on your application as a party or of its own motion (s 10)`
`s 16 yes` MEANS `yes: the court it is in may transfer it to that lower Northern Territory court, on your application as a party or of its own motion (s 16)`
`s 10 no` MEANS `no: s 10 and s 16 do not apply on these facts (the text's no: "this section applies if" fails)`

`notice yes` MEANS `yes: you gave the notice within the time the court directed (s 6(5)(b)); s 6(4)(a) is met once both Attorneys-General have it`
`notice pending` MEANS `not yet, but still in time: the time the court directed has not run out (s 6(5)(b))`
`notice late` MEANS `no: the notice was not given within the time the court directed (s 6(5)(b)); until both Attorneys-General have it, the Supreme Court cannot order that it keep the proceeding (s 6(4))`

§ `s 3, s 3A -- does this Act deal with my proceeding`

#ASSERT `s 3, s 3A -- does this Act deal with my proceeding` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: a civil proceeding, which this Act's rules on transfer, removal and appeal can reach (s 3)`
#ASSERT `s 3, s 3A -- does this Act deal with my proceeding` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: a criminal proceeding is not a "proceeding" under this Act (s 3(1), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 3, s 3A -- does this Act deal with my proceeding` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: this Act does not apply to the jurisdiction that Division 1 of Part 9.6A of the Corporations Act 2001 deals with (s 3A, the text's no)`
-- Both: criminal is answered first.
#ASSERT `s 3, s 3A -- does this Act deal with my proceeding` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: a criminal proceeding is not a "proceeding" under this Act (s 3(1), the text's no)`

-- The s 3(2) reading and the Northern Territory matter definition.
#ASSERT `a Supreme Court of another State, read with s 3(2)` `other SC`
#ASSERT `a Supreme Court of another State, read with s 3(2)` `FCWA`
#ASSERT NOT (`a Supreme Court of another State, read with s 3(2)` `NTSC`)
#ASSERT NOT (`a Supreme Court of another State, read with s 3(2)` `FCA`)
#ASSERT `a Northern Territory matter` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `a Northern Territory matter` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a Northern Territory matter` FALSE FALSE)

§ `s 4 -- can a court outside the Territory hear my matter`

-- A negligence claim under NT law, heard in the Supreme Court of Queensland.
#ASSERT `s 4 -- can a court outside the Territory hear my matter` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `a Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory` EQUALS `yes: that Supreme Court has and may exercise original and appellate jurisdiction in your Northern Territory matter (s 4(3))`
-- A matter removed under s 8 counts as a Northern Territory matter (s 3(1)(b)).
#ASSERT `s 4 -- can a court outside the Territory hear my matter` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `a Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory` EQUALS `yes: that Supreme Court has and may exercise original and appellate jurisdiction in your Northern Territory matter (s 4(3))`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- can a court outside the Territory hear my matter` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `a State Family Court of another State (the Family Court of Western Australia)` EQUALS `yes: that State Family Court has and may exercise original and appellate jurisdiction in your Northern Territory matter (s 4(4))`
-- s 4(1) and (2) are still in the NT text (finding 1).
#ASSERT `s 4 -- can a court outside the Territory hear my matter` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `the Federal Court` EQUALS `yes, as the text reads: the Federal Court has and may exercise original and appellate jurisdiction in your Northern Territory matter (s 4(1)); see NOTES.md finding 1 on whether a Territory law can give a federal court this jurisdiction`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- can a court outside the Territory hear my matter` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `the Family Court` EQUALS `yes, as the text reads: the Family Court has and may exercise original and appellate jurisdiction in your Northern Territory matter (s 4(2)); see NOTES.md finding 1 on whether a Territory law can give a federal court this jurisdiction`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- can a court outside the Territory hear my matter` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `a Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory` EQUALS `s 4 gives it nothing: your matter is not a Northern Territory matter (s 3(1)), and this Act does not say more (NOTHING-kind)`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- can a court outside the Territory hear my matter` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE `a Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory` EQUALS `no: s 4 gives no jurisdiction in criminal matters (s 4(5), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- can a court outside the Territory hear my matter` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `the Federal Court` EQUALS `no: this Act does not apply to the Corporations Act jurisdiction (s 3A, the text's no) -- s 4`

§ `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred`

-- s 5(1): NT Supreme Court to the Federal Court, on each finding (the NT s 5(1) has limb (iii)).
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `NTSC` `FCA` `MORE APPROPRIATE` EQUALS `s 5(1) yes`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `NTSC` `FCA` `INTERESTS OF JUSTICE` EQUALS `s 5(1) yes`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `NTSC` `FamCA` `NEITHER` EQUALS `s 5 no`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `NTSC` `FamCA` `MORE APPROPRIATE` EQUALS `s 5(1) yes`
-- s 5(2): NT Supreme Court to another Supreme Court, and to the Family Court of WA by s 3(2).
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `NTSC` `other SC` `INTERESTS OF JUSTICE` EQUALS `s 5(2) yes`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `NTSC` `FCWA` `MORE APPROPRIATE` EQUALS `s 5(2) yes`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `NTSC` `other SC` `NEITHER` EQUALS `s 5 no`
-- s 5(3): another Supreme Court (or the Family Court of WA) to the NT Supreme Court.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `other SC` `NTSC` `MORE APPROPRIATE` EQUALS `s 5(3) yes`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `FCWA` `NTSC` `INTERESTS OF JUSTICE` EQUALS `s 5(3) yes`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `other SC` `NTSC` `NEITHER` EQUALS `s 5 no`
-- s 5(4): a federal court to the NT Supreme Court.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `FCA` `NTSC` `INTERESTS OF JUSTICE` EQUALS `s 5(4) yes`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `FamCA` `NTSC` `MORE APPROPRIATE` EQUALS `s 5(4) yes`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `FamCA` `NTSC` `NEITHER` EQUALS `s 5 no`
-- s 5(5): between the two federal courts.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `FCA` `FamCA` `INTERESTS OF JUSTICE` EQUALS `s 5(5) yes`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `FamCA` `FCA` `MORE APPROPRIATE` EQUALS `s 5(5) yes`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `FCA` `FamCA` `NEITHER` EQUALS `s 5 no`
-- Routes this Act does not name.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `FCA` `FCA` `MORE APPROPRIATE` EQUALS `s 5 nothing`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `other SC` `FCA` `MORE APPROPRIATE` EQUALS `s 5 nothing`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `FCA` `other SC` `MORE APPROPRIATE` EQUALS `s 5 nothing`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `elsewhere` `NTSC` `MORE APPROPRIATE` EQUALS `s 5 nothing`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `NTSC` `NTSC` `MORE APPROPRIATE` EQUALS `s 5 nothing`
-- Outside the Act.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` TRUE FALSE `NTSC` `FCA` `MORE APPROPRIATE` EQUALS `not under Act s 5`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE TRUE `NTSC` `FCA` `MORE APPROPRIATE` EQUALS `not under Act s 5`

§ `s 5(6) -- must my related proceeding follow`

#ASSERT `s 5(6) -- must my related proceeding follow` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the court must transfer your related proceeding to the same court (s 5(6))`
#ASSERT `s 5(6) -- must my related proceeding follow` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 5(6) does not require it (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 5(6) -- must my related proceeding follow` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 5(6) does not require it (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 5(6) -- must my related proceeding follow` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 5(6) does not require it (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 5(6) -- must my related proceeding follow` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not under this Act: a criminal proceeding (s 3(1)) or the Corporations Act jurisdiction (s 3A) (the text's no) -- s 5(6)`

§ `s 5(7) -- can I apply for a transfer`

#ASSERT `s 5(7) -- can I apply for a transfer` `I am the plaintiff, applicant or claimant` EQUALS `yes: as a party you may apply for the transfer (s 5(7)); the court may also act of its own motion or on an Attorney-General's application`
#ASSERT `s 5(7) -- can I apply for a transfer` `I am the defendant or respondent` EQUALS `yes: as a party you may apply for the transfer (s 5(7)); the court may also act of its own motion or on an Attorney-General's application`
#ASSERT `s 5(7) -- can I apply for a transfer` `I have intervened in the proceeding` EQUALS `yes: a person who intervenes is a party (s 3(1)), so you may apply for the transfer (s 5(7))`
#ASSERT `s 5(7) -- can I apply for a transfer` `I am not a party and have not intervened` EQUALS `s 5(7) names no application by you: it names a party, the court of its own motion and the Attorneys-General (NOTHING-kind)`

§ `s 5(8) -- can my lawyer act for me in the new court`

#ASSERT `s 5(8) -- can my lawyer act for me in the new court` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: your lawyer may practise in the other court in this proceeding as in a federal court exercising federal jurisdiction (s 5(8))`
#ASSERT `s 5(8) -- can my lawyer act for me in the new court` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `s 5(8) gives your lawyer no right on these facts (the text's no: its "if" fails); the other court's own rules decide`
#ASSERT `s 5(8) -- can my lawyer act for me in the new court` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `s 5(8) gives your lawyer no right on these facts (the text's no: its "if" fails); the other court's own rules decide`
#ASSERT `s 5(8) -- can my lawyer act for me in the new court` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 5(8) gives your lawyer no right on these facts (the text's no: its "if" fails); the other court's own rules decide`

§ `s 6 -- must my special federal matter go to a federal court`

#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my special federal matter go to a federal court` FALSE FALSE TRUE `para a to e` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Supreme Court must transfer it to the Federal Court (s 6(1), (2)(a))`
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my special federal matter go to a federal court` FALSE FALSE TRUE `para ab` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Supreme Court must transfer it to whichever of the Family Court of Australia and the Family Court of Western Australia it thinks appropriate in the circumstances (s 6(1), (2)(b))`
-- Finding 3: a paragraph s 6(2) does not name.
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my special federal matter go to a federal court` FALSE FALSE TRUE `para unnamed` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes, it must be transferred (s 6(1)), but s 6(2) names no court for that paragraph of the definition (NOTHING-kind as to where)`
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my special federal matter go to a federal court` FALSE FALSE TRUE `para a to e` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: the Supreme Court has ordered that it decide the proceeding itself (s 6(1), (3); the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my special federal matter go to a federal court` FALSE FALSE TRUE `para a to e` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 6 does not apply to this appeal in the Full Court of the Supreme Court, because the court below made an order under s 6(3) (s 6(9), the text's no)`
-- s 6(9) is answered before an order kept (fork F5).
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my special federal matter go to a federal court` FALSE FALSE TRUE `para ab` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 6 does not apply to this appeal in the Full Court of the Supreme Court, because the court below made an order under s 6(3) (s 6(9), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my special federal matter go to a federal court` FALSE FALSE TRUE `no SFM` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 6 does not arise: no special federal matter, or the proceeding is not pending in the Supreme Court (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my special federal matter go to a federal court` FALSE FALSE FALSE `para a to e` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 6 does not arise: no special federal matter, or the proceeding is not pending in the Supreme Court (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my special federal matter go to a federal court` TRUE FALSE TRUE `para a to e` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not under this Act: a criminal proceeding (s 3(1)) or the Corporations Act jurisdiction (s 3A) (the text's no) -- s 6`
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my special federal matter go to a federal court` FALSE TRUE TRUE `para a to e` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not under this Act: a criminal proceeding (s 3(1)) or the Corporations Act jurisdiction (s 3A) (the text's no) -- s 6`

§ `s 6(3) -- can the Supreme Court keep my special federal matter`

#ASSERT `s 6(3) -- can the Supreme Court keep my special federal matter` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the Supreme Court may order that it decide the proceeding itself (s 6(3)); it must act on the general rule that special federal matters go to the federal courts, and weigh any Attorney-General's submission (s 6(6))`
-- Notice to one Attorney-General only (edge).
#ASSERT `s 6(3) -- can the Supreme Court keep my special federal matter` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: not before written notice of the special federal matter has been given to both the Commonwealth and the Northern Territory Attorney-General (s 6(4)(a), the text's no); the court may adjourn and direct a party to give it (s 6(5))`
#ASSERT `s 6(3) -- can the Supreme Court keep my special federal matter` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: not before written notice of the special federal matter has been given to both the Commonwealth and the Northern Territory Attorney-General (s 6(4)(a), the text's no); the court may adjourn and direct a party to give it (s 6(5))`
#ASSERT `s 6(3) -- can the Supreme Court keep my special federal matter` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: not before a reasonable time has passed since the notice for the Attorneys-General to consider making submissions (s 6(4)(b), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 6(3) -- can the Supreme Court keep my special federal matter` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: the court is not satisfied that there are special reasons, other than the parties' convenience, for it to decide the proceeding (s 6(3), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 6(3) -- can the Supreme Court keep my special federal matter` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `s 6(3) does not arise: no special federal matter pending in the Supreme Court (the text's no)`

§ `s 6(5)(b) -- the notice the court directed`

-- The regulative rule alone, 28 days allowed: day 0, the last day (28), the day after (29).
#ASSERT `s 6(5)(b) -- notice on this day is in time` 28 0
#ASSERT `s 6(5)(b) -- notice on this day is in time` 28 28
#ASSERT NOT (`s 6(5)(b) -- notice on this day is in time` 28 29)

-- Directed on 1 March 2026 with 28 days: the last day is 29 March 2026.
#ASSERT `s 6(5)(b) -- have I given the notice in time` `1 Mar 2026` 28 TRUE `1 Mar 2026` `31 Mar 2026` EQUALS `notice yes`
#ASSERT `s 6(5)(b) -- have I given the notice in time` `1 Mar 2026` 28 TRUE `15 Mar 2026` `31 Mar 2026` EQUALS `notice yes`
#ASSERT `s 6(5)(b) -- have I given the notice in time` `1 Mar 2026` 28 TRUE `29 Mar 2026` `31 Mar 2026` EQUALS `notice yes`
#ASSERT `s 6(5)(b) -- have I given the notice in time` `1 Mar 2026` 28 TRUE `30 Mar 2026` `31 Mar 2026` EQUALS `notice late`
-- A notice given before the direction counts (fork F7).
#ASSERT `s 6(5)(b) -- have I given the notice in time` `1 Mar 2026` 28 TRUE `28 Feb 2026` `31 Mar 2026` EQUALS `notice yes`
-- Not given: today the last day, then the day after.
#ASSERT `s 6(5)(b) -- have I given the notice in time` `1 Mar 2026` 28 FALSE `1 Mar 2026` `29 Mar 2026` EQUALS `notice pending`
#ASSERT `s 6(5)(b) -- have I given the notice in time` `1 Mar 2026` 28 FALSE `1 Mar 2026` `30 Mar 2026` EQUALS `notice late`
#ASSERT `s 6(5)(b) -- have I given the notice in time` `1 Mar 2026` 28 FALSE `1 Mar 2026` `15 Mar 2026` EQUALS `notice pending`

§ `s 6(7) -- urgent interim relief`

#ASSERT `s 6(7) -- can the Supreme Court still give me urgent interim relief` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: nothing in s 6 stops the Supreme Court granting urgent interlocutory relief, as it is in the interests of justice (s 6(7))`
#ASSERT `s 6(7) -- can the Supreme Court still give me urgent interim relief` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 6(7) does not save it: the court does not find the relief in the interests of justice (the text's no: its "if" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 6(7) -- can the Supreme Court still give me urgent interim relief` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `s 6(7) does not reach it: it speaks only of urgent relief of an interlocutory nature (NOTHING-kind)`

§ `s 6(8), s 7(7) -- is the decision invalid`

#ASSERT `s 6(8), s 7(7) -- is the decision invalid because it was not transferred` `the Supreme Court decided a special federal matter without an order under s 6(3)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not invalid for that reason: nothing in s 6 invalidates the decision (s 6(8))`
#ASSERT `s 6(8), s 7(7) -- is the decision invalid because it was not transferred` `the Supreme Court decided a special federal matter without the s 6(4) notice having been given` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not invalid for that reason: nothing in s 6 invalidates the decision (s 6(8))`
#ASSERT `s 6(8), s 7(7) -- is the decision invalid because it was not transferred` `the Supreme Court decided a special federal matter without an order under s 6(3)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `this Act does not say: s 6(8) and s 7(7) save only a decision made through inadvertence or, for s 7, after the Full Court went on under s 7(6) (NOTHING-kind)`
-- s 7(6) going on does not save an s 6 decision.
#ASSERT `s 6(8), s 7(7) -- is the decision invalid because it was not transferred` `the Supreme Court decided a special federal matter without an order under s 6(3)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `this Act does not say: s 6(8) and s 7(7) save only a decision made through inadvertence or, for s 7, after the Full Court went on under s 7(6) (NOTHING-kind)`
#ASSERT `s 6(8), s 7(7) -- is the decision invalid because it was not transferred` `the Full Court of the Supreme Court decided an appeal that s 7(4) sends to a Full Court of the Federal Court or the Family Court` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not invalid for that reason: nothing in s 7 invalidates the decision (s 7(7))`
#ASSERT `s 6(8), s 7(7) -- is the decision invalid because it was not transferred` `the Full Court of the Supreme Court decided an appeal that s 7(4) sends to a Full Court of the Federal Court or the Family Court` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not invalid for that reason: nothing in s 7 invalidates the decision (s 7(7))`
#ASSERT `s 6(8), s 7(7) -- is the decision invalid because it was not transferred` `the Full Court of the Supreme Court decided an appeal that s 7(4) sends to a Full Court of the Federal Court or the Family Court` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `this Act does not say: s 6(8) and s 7(7) save only a decision made through inadvertence or, for s 7, after the Full Court went on under s 7(6) (NOTHING-kind)`

