#ASSERT `s 7 -- where can my appeal go` FALSE FALSE `some other decision` `NT Full Court` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `appeal nothing`
#ASSERT `s 7 -- where can my appeal go` TRUE FALSE `NTSC judge` `NT Full Court` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not under this Act: a criminal proceeding (s 3(1)) or the Corporations Act jurisdiction (s 3A) (the text's no) -- s 7`

§ `s 7(6) -- must the Full Court send my appeal on`

#ASSERT `s 7(6) -- must the Full Court send my appeal to a federal Full Court` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Full Court of the Supreme Court must transfer it to the Full Court of the Federal Court or of the Family Court, as the case requires (s 7(6))`
#ASSERT `s 7(6) -- must the Full Court send my appeal to a federal Full Court` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: the interests of justice require the Full Court of the Supreme Court to go on and decide it (s 7(6)); its decision is not invalid under s 7 (s 7(7))`
#ASSERT `s 7(6) -- must the Full Court send my appeal to a federal Full Court` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 7(6) does not arise (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 7(6) -- must the Full Court send my appeal to a federal Full Court` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 7(6) does not arise (the text's no: its "where" fails)`

§ `s 8 -- removal to the Supreme Court`

#ASSERT `s 8 -- can my proceeding be removed to the Supreme Court` FALSE FALSE `a Northern Territory court other than the Supreme Court` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Supreme Court may order it removed to itself, on your application as a party or of its own motion (s 8(1)); this Act then treats it as pending in the Supreme Court (s 8(2)), which may later send it back if it considers that appropriate (s 8(3))`
#ASSERT `s 8 -- can my proceeding be removed to the Supreme Court` FALSE FALSE `a tribunal established by or under an Act` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the Supreme Court may order it removed to itself, on your application as a party or of its own motion (s 8(1)); this Act then treats it as pending in the Supreme Court (s 8(2)), which may later send it back if it considers that appropriate (s 8(3))`
#ASSERT `s 8 -- can my proceeding be removed to the Supreme Court` FALSE FALSE `a Northern Territory court other than the Supreme Court` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 8 does not allow removal on these facts (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 8 -- can my proceeding be removed to the Supreme Court` FALSE FALSE `the Supreme Court, or a court outside the Northern Territory` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 8 does not allow removal on these facts (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 8 -- can my proceeding be removed to the Supreme Court` FALSE TRUE `a Northern Territory court other than the Supreme Court` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not under this Act: a criminal proceeding (s 3(1)) or the Corporations Act jurisdiction (s 3A) (the text's no) -- s 8`

