#ASSERT `s 10, s 16 -- can my consumer law case go to a lower court` FALSE FALSE `NTSC` `no consumer law` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `s 10 no`
#ASSERT `s 10, s 16 -- can my consumer law case go to a lower court` FALSE FALSE `elsewhere` `ACL listed` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `s 10 no`
#ASSERT `s 10, s 16 -- can my consumer law case go to a lower court` FALSE FALSE `NTSC` `ACL listed` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `s 10 no`
#ASSERT `s 10, s 16 -- can my consumer law case go to a lower court` FALSE FALSE `NTSC` `ACL listed` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `s 10 no`
#ASSERT `s 10, s 16 -- can my consumer law case go to a lower court` FALSE FALSE `NTSC` `TPA Part V` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 10 no`
#ASSERT `s 10, s 16 -- can my consumer law case go to a lower court` TRUE FALSE `NTSC` `ACL listed` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not under this Act: a criminal proceeding (s 3(1)) or the Corporations Act jurisdiction (s 3A) (the text's no) -- s 10, s 16`

§ `s 11, s 12 -- applicable law, steps taken, costs`

#ASSERT `s 11(1) -- which law will the court apply to my claim` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the written and unwritten law of the other State or Territory under whose written law your right of action arises (s 11(1)(b)); evidence and procedure as the court considers appropriate, from rules a superior court in Australia or an external Territory applies (s 11(1)(c))`
-- (b) comes before (a) and (2), even in a federal court.
#ASSERT `s 11(1) -- which law will the court apply to my claim` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the written and unwritten law of the other State or Territory under whose written law your right of action arises (s 11(1)(b)); evidence and procedure as the court considers appropriate, from rules a superior court in Australia or an external Territory applies (s 11(1)(c))`
#ASSERT `s 11(1) -- which law will the court apply to my claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the law in force in the State or Territory where the court is sitting, including its choice of law rules (s 11(1)(a)); evidence and procedure as the court considers appropriate, from rules a superior court in Australia or an external Territory applies (s 11(1)(c))`
#ASSERT `s 11(1) -- which law will the court apply to my claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the law in force in the State or Territory where a matter in your proceeding was first commenced in or transferred to the Federal Court or the Family Court, including its choice of law rules (s 11(1)(a), (2)); evidence and procedure as the court considers appropriate, from rules a superior court in Australia or an external Territory applies (s 11(1)(c))`
#ASSERT `s 11(1) -- which law will the court apply to my claim` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `s 11(1) does not apply: the court will not be exercising cross-vested jurisdiction (the text's no: its "where" fails); this Act does not say which law applies`

#ASSERT `s 11(3) -- do the steps already taken count in the new court` TRUE EQUALS `yes: the new court deals with the proceeding as if the steps taken in the old court, including its orders, had been taken in the new court, subject to any order of the new court (s 11(3))`
#ASSERT `s 11(3) -- do the steps already taken count in the new court` FALSE EQUALS `s 11(3) does not apply: the proceeding was not transferred or removed (the text's no: its "where" fails)`

#ASSERT `s 12 -- can the new court order the costs of the earlier stage` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the new court may make an order about the costs of the proceeding before the transfer or removal (s 12)`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- can the new court order the costs of the earlier stage` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: those costs have already been dealt with by another court (s 12, the text's no: its "if" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- can the new court order the costs of the earlier stage` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 12 does not apply: the proceeding was not transferred or removed (the text's no: its "where" fails)`

§ `s 13, s 14 -- appeals from transfer decisions, enforcement`

#ASSERT `s 13 -- can I appeal that decision` `a decision about transferring or removing my proceeding under this Act` EQUALS `no: no appeal lies from a decision about the transfer or removal of a proceeding under this Act (s 13(a), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 13 -- can I appeal that decision` `a decision under s 11(1) about which rules of evidence and procedure apply` EQUALS `no: no appeal lies from a decision about which rules of evidence and procedure apply under s 11(1) (s 13(b), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 13 -- can I appeal that decision` `some other decision in my proceeding` EQUALS `s 13 does not bar an appeal from it; whether one lies is for other law (NOTHING-kind)`

#ASSERT `s 14(1), (2) -- can I enforce the judgment in the Northern Territory` `FCA` TRUE EQUALS `yes: the judgment is enforceable in the Northern Territory as if given entirely in that federal court's own jurisdiction (s 14(1))`
#ASSERT `s 14(1), (2) -- can I enforce the judgment in the Northern Territory` `FamCA` TRUE EQUALS `yes: the judgment is enforceable in the Northern Territory as if given entirely in that federal court's own jurisdiction (s 14(1))`
#ASSERT `s 14(1), (2) -- can I enforce the judgment in the Northern Territory` `NTSC` TRUE EQUALS `yes: the judgment is enforceable in the Northern Territory as if given entirely in the Supreme Court's own jurisdiction (s 14(2))`
#ASSERT `s 14(1), (2) -- can I enforce the judgment in the Northern Territory` `NTSC` FALSE EQUALS `s 14 does not reach it: it covers only a judgment of the Federal Court, the Family Court or the Supreme Court of the Northern Territory given in whole or in part in cross-vested jurisdiction (NOTHING-kind)`
#ASSERT `s 14(1), (2) -- can I enforce the judgment in the Northern Territory` `other SC` TRUE EQUALS `s 14 does not reach it: it covers only a judgment of the Federal Court, the Family Court or the Supreme Court of the Northern Territory given in whole or in part in cross-vested jurisdiction (NOTHING-kind)`

#ASSERT `s 14(3) -- does a Territory law that speaks of the Supreme Court cover the other court` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: that provision is read as referring to the court that did the thing (s 14(3))`
#ASSERT `s 14(3) -- does a Territory law that speaks of the Supreme Court cover the other court` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 14(3) does not reach a law relating to the enforcement of judgments (s 14(3)(a), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 14(3) -- does a Territory law that speaks of the Supreme Court cover the other court` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `s 14(3) does not apply on these facts (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 14(3) -- does a Territory law that speaks of the Supreme Court cover the other court` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 14(3) does not apply on these facts (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
